# Ponytail (project-local)

This repository vendors [Ponytail](https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail) under `.cursor/skills/ponytail/`.

For substantive coding work (implement, fix, refactor, review, dependency choices), read and follow:

`.cursor/skills/ponytail/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md`

Other skills in the same tree:

| Skill | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Review a diff | `.cursor/skills/ponytail/skills/ponytail-review/SKILL.md` |
| Repo quality audit | `.cursor/skills/ponytail/skills/ponytail-audit/SKILL.md` |
| Technical debt ledger | `.cursor/skills/ponytail/skills/ponytail-debt/SKILL.md` |
| Impact scoreboard | `.cursor/skills/ponytail/skills/ponytail-gain/SKILL.md` |
| Quick reference | `.cursor/skills/ponytail/skills/ponytail-help/SKILL.md` |

Use the `Read` tool on these paths (same as Superpowers). In Cursor chat you can also attach skills manually or send `/ponytail lite`, `/ponytail full`, `/ponytail ultra`, or `/ponytail off` as plain messages when [project hooks](#cursor-hooks) are installed.

## Cursor hooks (optional)

Project-level hooks live in `.cursor/hooks.json` when installed. They inject the active Ponytail level at session start and track `/ponytail` mode switches. Re-install after moving the submodule:

```bash
node .cursor/skills/ponytail/scripts/cursor-hooks.js install --project
```

Do not add `.cursor/rules/ponytail.mdc` from the submodule while using these hooks; Ponytail treats the always-on rule and hooks as alternatives.

## Precedence

`AGENTS.md` and direct user messages override Ponytail. Ponytail and Superpowers can both apply; resolve conflicts in favor of the user and this repo’s `AGENTS.md`.
